- The sequence must be non-increasing (precondition)
- The element `x` is correctly inserted into the sequence (postconditions)
- The indices `k` are correct and meet the order properties (postconditions)
- No infinite loops (proven by the `decreases` clause)

The `Test` method verifies that both methods produce the same results for the same inputs, confirming that the enhancement doesn't break correctness while preventing infinite recursion.
